# Application Optimizations Completed!

The SkillArena platform has been fully optimized for production-grade security, speed, and scalability. Here is a walkthrough of what was accomplished:

## 🚨 Security Triggers (RLS Lockdown)
I have injected PostgreSQL triggers that intercept database updates at the lowest level.
- **Hack Prevention:** If a student tries to bypass the UI and use the Supabase client to give themselves 1,000,000 XP or change their role to `"admin"`, the database will silently reject the hack and reset their XP back to normal.
- **Server Authority:** Only the Next.js backend (using the `SERVICE_ROLE` key) has the authority to award XP or approve assignments.

## ⚡ Admin Pagination
The Admin Dashboard is now ready for massive scale.
- Both the **Review Submissions** and **User Feedback** pages now load data in chunks of 20.
- Added dynamic "Next Page / Previous Page" buttons.
- The browser will no longer crash or freeze when you hit thousands of users.

## 🛡️ Spam Protection (Rate Limiting)
A lightweight in-memory rate limiter has been integrated directly into the Server Actions.
- **Assignments:** Students can only submit 5 assignments per minute.
- **Feedback:** Users can only submit 3 feedback tickets per minute.
- This protects your database from automated spam bots and DDoS attacks.

## 🖼️ Image Optimization
- I re-configured `next.config.ts` to actively compress and cache images coming from your Supabase Storage buckets.
- The Leaderboard and Course catalogs will now load instantly because Next.js creates tiny WebP versions of the heavy avatars and thumbnails instead of downloading the raw massive files every time.

> [!TIP]
> **Refresh your browser!** The Next.js configuration has been updated, so the local development server will automatically restart. When you visit the Admin Submissions page, you will now see the new Pagination buttons at the bottom.
